        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF142 <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Animation/commitStyles\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Animation/commitStyles()</code></a> allows animations to capture the final styles without specifying a <code class=\"notranslate\">fill</code> in latest spec.<br>\nThis updates the docs.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that this is in draft. I just found out that there is no way to know whether your browser supports this, so I need to invert docs to show the old way first.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3249106813\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40482\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40482/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40482\">#40482</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40585",
            "title": "FF142 Animation.commitStyles() automatically fills values",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-01T07:26:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-01T07:24:15.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112591951?u=83251e0d8e8f801faef99cc68533e148a728784b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add a “Using your Wasm in an ES 6 bundler” section that shows how to import the generated JavaScript glue file as a side effect and how to emit a factory‐style ES 6 module with Emscripten flags <code class=\"notranslate\">MODULARIZE</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">EXPORT_ES6</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The following changes were made because, just as the issue stated, Most modern web projects use ES 6 modules and a bundler (webpack, Vite, Rollup, etc.). Readers need a simple recipe for integrating Emscripten’s output into their build system without extra loader configuration.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Sources I have used for the edits, along with the issue description in github:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Emscripten <code class=\"notranslate\">MODULARIZE</code> option (produces a factory function):<br>\n<a href=\"https://emscripten.org/docs/tools_reference/emcc.html#modularize\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://emscripten.org/docs/tools_reference/emcc.html#modularize</a></li>\n<li>Emscripten <code class=\"notranslate\">EXPORT_ES6</code> option (emits an ES 6 module):<br>\n<a href=\"https://emscripten.org/docs/tools_reference/emcc.html#export_es6\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://emscripten.org/docs/tools_reference/emcc.html#export_es6</a></li>\n<li>Example of using Emscripten output with npm and bundlers:<br>\n<a href=\"https://web.dev/wasm-npm/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://web.dev/wasm-npm/</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #40526.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3261853511\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40526\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40526/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40526\">#40526</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
