        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF142 supports the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Prioritized_Task_Scheduling_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">Prioritized Task Scheduling AP</a> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1966997\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1966997</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note and removes the experimental features entry.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in  <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3249171453\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40484\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40484/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40484\">#40484</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40553",
            "title": "FF142 Relnote/Expr: Prioritized task scheduling API",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-28T02:18:03.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-28T02:15:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #37665.\">Fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2791137356\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37665\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/37665/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37665\">#37665</a>, and its two linked issues, which as I work through this PR realized are not actually duplicates of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2791137356\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37665\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/37665/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37665\">#37665</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40548",
            "title": "Provide more guidelines about labeling input",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-02T06:47:15.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-27T12:15:24.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">I've been long bothered by the fact that \"CSSOM view\" is not a real API group on MDN. It makes our IA extremely awkward because existing references either have get the sidebar of its owner interface (such as \"DOM\" for <code class=\"notranslate\">Window</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Document</code> extensions, or \"UI events\" for <code class=\"notranslate\">MouseEvent</code> extensions) or be fakely labeled as \"CSSOM\". \"Visual Viewport API\" is also not a real spec anymore. So we basically hacked around the whole issue of lacking a proper API group.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Meanwhile we do have a \"CSSOM view\" landing page, but it's confusingly categorized as CSS, which means it cannot be used as the landing page of a web API group, because of the way our groupdata.json works. All the other CSS specs that define JS bindings, such as CSSOM, CSS Typed OM, etc. are under web API, so I think this should be no exception: the CSS docs should be left to the CSS language proper, not for JS bindings.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm adding the groupdata for the new interfaces only. There are too many interface extensions and I'm not interested in updating their sidebars in this PR, although a future one might.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40547",
            "title": "Move CSSOM view module under API/",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-29T02:02:44.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-27T11:10:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74392116?u=4129621f9e965839bd287d5e557fe87b816cf331&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The change mainly aims for better accuracy to describe CSS value processing flow according to the specification.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The previous version sometimes used incorrect terminology and descriptions, which will ultimately lead differences between mdn and the specs.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">e.g.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>CSS property value result will not come only from specificity - it will be the result of the entire cascade process</li>\n<li>\"specified values\" were mostly used incorrectly/confused with \"declared values\" - \"specified values\" result from the defaulting process after cascading, but the previous version didn't make this clear</li>\n<li>The document mainly described the stages after the <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/css-cascade-4/#defaulting\" rel=\"nofollow\">Defaulting process</a>, even though the terminology and phases <em>before</em> Defaulting<br>\n(which are Filtering, Cascading, and related terms) are necessary to make <em>after</em>-Defaulting values understandable. Omitting the before-Defaulting process essentially leads to misworded descriptions.</li>\n<li>Initial value shouldn't be listed as a value processing stage according to the spec - it is the terminology used in the specified value resolution process</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The change also includes some typo/wording updates, which will make the description more accurate or simpler.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The changes ensure compliance with:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/css-syntax-3/\" rel=\"nofollow\">CSS Syntax Module Level 3</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/css-cascade-4/\" rel=\"nofollow\">CSS Cascading and Inheritance Level 4</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40546",
            "title": "Refine CSS Value Processing document",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-29T16:17:03.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-27T10:58:07.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "sakupi01",
                "url": "https://github.com/sakupi01"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #25571.\">Fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1637681369\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/25571\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/25571/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/25571\">#25571</a>. Wondering if you could advise <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/padenot/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/padenot\">@padenot</a>—thanks!</p>",
